ings AI-powered code suggestions to these development environments\n   - [Source: GitLab Blog](https://about.gitlab.com/blog/gitlab-jetbrains-neovim-plugins/)\n\n### AI Coding Agents for Multiple Platforms\n\n2. **Amp Code**\n   - A coding agent that integrates with multiple platforms including Neovim, VS Code, and JetBrains\n   - Provides terminal and editor integration\n   - [Source: Zencoder AI](https://zencoder.ai/blog/ai-coding-agent-for-neovim)\n\n3. **Cline (VS Code Extension)**\n   - AI-powered agentic coding assistance for VS Code\n   - Features a built-in MCP Marketplace for enhanced functionality\n   - [Source: Medium](https://ricardo-castellanos-herreros.medium.com/best-ai-coding-extensions-for-ides-82f3e31290a9)\n\n4. **Windsurf Plugins**\n   - Supports JetBrains, VS Code, Visual Studio, Vim, NeoVim, Jupyter, and Chrome\n   - Provides AI-powered coding assistance across multiple IDEs\n   - [Source: Windsurf Documentation](https://docs.windsurf.com/plugins/getting-started)\n\n### Neovim AI Agent Plugins\n\n5. **OpenAI and Multi-LLM Integrations**\n   - Various plugins for Neovim supporting ChatGPT, Codex, Gemini, Grok, and multiple LLMs\n   - Plugins for documentation generation and AI-assisted coding\n   - [Source: Neovim Plugin List](https://yutkat.github.io/my-neovim-pluginlist/ai.html)\n\n6. **Specialized Neovim AI Plugins**\n   - Plugins that allow seamless integration with AI agents without leaving the editor\n   - Chat-based code interaction similar to Cursor AI IDE experience\n   - [Source: Awesome Neovim](https://github.com/rockerBOO/awesome-neovim)\n\n### Industry Trends\n\nThe search results show a clear trend toward multi-platform AI agent support, with tools like Amp Code and Windsurf explicitly targeting VS Code, JetBrains, and Neovim simultaneously. This suggests that by May 2026, developers will have increasingly unified AI agent experiences across different editor ecosystems.\n\n**Note**: I encountered rate limiting issues when searching